1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,469
The Tiny Birthday Secret.

3
00:00:03,469 --> 00:00:05,573
Mom's birthday is tomorrow.

4
00:00:05,573 --> 00:00:10,698
Emma has offered to help me make a big card, and Ben has offered to help by asking a lot of questions.

5
00:00:10,698 --> 00:00:12,687
I call Emma after dinner.

6
00:00:12,914 --> 00:00:14,333
What time should I come over?

7
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:16,207
Ten tomorrow morning.

8
00:00:16,207 --> 00:00:18,655
Dad's taking Mom out for breakfast.

9
00:00:18,655 --> 00:00:21,707
We'll have about an hour to finish the card and set the table.

10
00:00:21,988 --> 00:00:23,523
Are we having cake?

11
00:00:23,523 --> 00:00:25,232
Is the cake a secret?

12
00:00:25,232 --> 00:00:27,023
Can I taste the secret?

13
00:00:27,292 --> 00:00:29,932
Everything is a secret until Mom gets home.

14
00:00:29,932 --> 00:00:31,442
Don't tell her yet.

15
00:00:31,732 --> 00:00:33,392
I'll keep it a secret.

16
00:00:33,392 --> 00:00:35,538
I am excellent at not talking.

17
00:00:35,812 --> 00:00:38,639
He proves this by talking for another five minutes.

18
00:00:38,639 --> 00:00:42,212
The next morning, Emma arrives with colored paper and stickers.

19
00:00:42,212 --> 00:00:44,722
We write little messages inside the card.

20
00:00:44,722 --> 00:00:47,649
Mine says thank you for helping me even when I'm grumpy.

21
00:00:47,882 --> 00:00:49,134
That's a good message.

22
00:00:49,134 --> 00:00:52,186
Mine says happy birthday to the best pancake maker I know.

23
00:00:52,468 --> 00:00:54,868
Mine says I love you more than cake.

24
00:00:54,868 --> 00:00:56,472
Is that believable?

25
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:58,463
Very generous of you.

26
00:00:58,463 --> 00:01:01,859
We hear the front door, so we hide the card behind our backs.

27
00:01:01,859 --> 00:01:04,359
Mom walks into the kitchen and stops.

28
00:01:04,636 --> 00:01:07,242
Why is everybody standing so strangely?

29
00:01:07,468 --> 00:01:08,816
No reason.

30
00:01:08,816 --> 00:01:11,430
Definitely not because of a giant card.

31
00:01:11,716 --> 00:01:13,606
We all laugh and hold it up.

32
00:01:13,606 --> 00:01:15,116
Surprise!

33
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,481
Mom reads every message slowly.

34
00:01:17,481 --> 00:01:21,147
Then she hugs us, including our terrible little secret keeper.

35
00:01:21,147 --> 00:01:24,418
The card is slightly crooked, but her smile is perfect.
